~ Block-scope join (see docs/concurrency/README.md): a `< >` block joins every launch it
~ made before it returns — `allSettled`, so a launch bound to a name the block never reads
~ again still runs to completion rather than being left running past the block's own return.
~
~ `hearsay` below is exactly that: launched, then never read again. `testimony` is what the
~ block actually needs. With no input piped (the examples gate points stdin at EOF), both
~ launches settle to "" — the join runs regardless of what either yields, so a passing exit
~ code here is evidence the unused launch settled, not proof of any particular value.

<< core.io
<< core.test

^ = () -> Num => <
  hearsay = @readStdin()          ~ launched — the block joins it even though it goes unread
  testimony = @readStdin()
  assert(testimony, equals(""))   ~ end-of-input; forces `testimony` (the join settles `hearsay` too)
  0
>
